==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm}} {{term|maddoc}}, from an unrecorded {{etyl|ang}} form corresponding to Old Norse {{term|maðkr}} (whence dialectal English {{term|mawk}}, Danish {{term|madike}}, Swedish {{term|mask}}), originally a diminutive of the {{proto|Germanic|maða-|worm}} (whence Old English {{term|maþa}})

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmadək/}}

Of Celtic origin meaning 'good', derived from Madog.